1. Global informations about Flut!

Flut! is a strategy boardgame with

 - multiportsupport
 - up to 50 games
 - variable size
 - 2-6 players in a game (no teamgames)
 - 1 turn a day with min. 12 hrs pause (like GW)
 - Rankings
 - News Report (newspaper with ended games)
 - Hall of Flut
 - Walls (one per game and one global)
 - Ansis by Miracle (tHe fAMoUs!)



2. Documentation



2.1 Indroduction



2.1.1 Game-theory

Please  read  EXACTLY!   In the next 30 lines you get a lot (really a LOT!)
information about the game-theory of Flut!

Flut is a strategy-game.

 Your  looking  at the playground from top, filled with a definit number of
buckets.   They  have  to  be filled!  Every player gets his own colour for
filling  these  buckets for a third.  You can only fill in empty buckets or
in buckets of your own colour.

 If  a  bucket  is  full,  it floods.  And it floods the buckets at top, at
bottom,  to  the  right and to the left with its colour, again for a third.
(at X-Flut flooding works diagonal)
 
Flooded  buckets  are  filled  for  a  third with the colour of the filling
player.   Or  automatically  they  take  the colour they were flooded with.
Real chainreactions are possible here.

 Buckets that are allready  full,  won`t  be  changed anymore.

 Each  turn,  you  get  a  third  of  a  bucket with colour to fill in.  In
contrary  to  GW  it  will  not  be  multiplied with the number of days not
playing.  At Flut the number of fillings become double after three days not
playing - thats all!  - nothing more!

The game ends, when one player is unreachable in front.



2.1.2 Points

One point for every filled bucket (three thirds)!

When a game ends, the winner gets a bonus of:

  X_Size*Y_Size*Players/6 ( max. 11*11*6/6=121 points)

and the looser a deduction of:

  X_Size*Y_Size/6 ( max. 11*11/6=20 points)

 This  ensures that the size of playground and the number of players become
an important factor, and not only the number of games you join.

 At 1000 points you enter the "Hall of Fame" and the scores restart.



2.1.3 Choises at joining

At gamestart following values will be asked:

- X-SIZE   : X-size of playground
- Y-SIZE   : Y-size of playground

- DIRECTION: the direction the buckets will flood (x=diagonal n=normal)

- BORDERS  : playgroundmargins are borders (y=yep) or
           : playgroundmargins are no borders and you continue on opposite
             side (n=no)

- PLAYERS  : number of players (possible:2-6)



